#: ../../advanced/providers.md:1
msgid "Custom Providers"
msgstr "Custom Providers"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:3
msgid "Language Check supports external checker binaries that communicate via stdin/stdout JSON."
msgstr "Language Check supports external checker binaries that communicate via stdin/stdout JSON."

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:6
msgid "[Vale](https://vale.sh/) has built-in first-class support — use `engines.vale: true` instead of registering it as a custom provider. See [Vale Setup](../guide/vale-setup.md)."
msgstr "[Vale](https://vale.sh/) has built-in first-class support — use `engines.vale: true` instead of registering it as a custom provider. See [Vale Setup](../guide/vale-setup.md)."

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:10
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuration"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:12
msgid "Register external providers in `.languagecheck.yaml`:"
msgstr "Register external providers in `.languagecheck.yaml`:"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:26
msgid "`extensions` and `languages` are different questions, and a provider is skipped when either excludes the document. Leaving one out means \"all of them\"."
msgstr "`extensions` and `languages` are different questions, and a provider is skipped when either excludes the document. Leaving one out means \"all of them\"."

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:29
msgid "Declaring `languages` matters more than it looks: a provider that claims every language makes the checker believe the passage was checked, which suppresses the report saying nothing could read it — so a provider that only speaks English silently hides the fact that a Hebrew paragraph went unchecked."
msgstr "Declaring `languages` matters more than it looks: a provider that claims every language makes the checker believe the passage was checked, which suppresses the report saying nothing could read it — so a provider that only speaks English silently hides the fact that a Hebrew paragraph went unchecked."

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:34
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr "Protocol"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:36
msgid "Request (stdin)"
msgstr "Request (stdin)"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:38
msgid "The provider receives a JSON object on stdin:"
msgstr "The provider receives a JSON object on stdin:"

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:47
msgid "`language_id` is the **natural** language being checked as a BCP-47 tag, not the markup format — `en-US`, `de-DE`, `fr`. The document's markup is not sent; declare `extensions` if the provider needs to know it."
msgstr "`language_id` is the **natural** language being checked as a BCP-47 tag, not the markup format — `en-US`, `de-DE`, `fr`. The document's markup is not sent; declare `extensions` if the provider needs to know it."

#: ../../advanced/providers.md:51
msgid "`text` is one extracted prose range, not the whole file. A document is checked range by range, so a provider is invoked once per range and its byte offsets are relative to the text it was given."
msgstr "`text` is one extracted prose range, not the whole file. A document is checked range by range, so a provider is invoked once per range and its byte offsets are relative to the text it was given."

